{
  "table_id": "Table_S31",
  "display_number": "S31",
  "title": "Supplementary Table S31. Co-pollutant mutual-adjustment sensitivity analysis.",
  "panel": "",
  "panel_title": "",
  "notes_before": [],
  "notes_after": [
    "Note. Estimates are adjusted mean BAA differences per buffer-specific IQR from unweighted WeMix mixed-effects models with participant-level random intercepts, robust (sandwich) covariance and the primary covariate set. The primary dual-exposure model includes EVI within residential buffers and O₃. Sensitivity models additionally include the supplied current-year PM₂.₅ field, the supplied current-year NO₂ field, or both simultaneously. PM₂.₅ and NO₂ are treated as current-year co-pollutant fields and are not interpreted as validated four-year exposure means. Complete-case model frames were used; N therefore varies across specifications. This table is supportive and does not establish a causal or independent O₃ association.",
    "Abbreviations: BAA, biological age acceleration; CI, confidence interval; EVI, enhanced vegetation index; IQR, interquartile range; NO₂, nitrogen dioxide; O₃, ozone; PM₂.₅, particulate matter with aerodynamic diameter ≤2.5 μm."
  ],
